Root cause: Owl daemon at /Users/mihirkanzariya/.nvm/versions/node/v24.13.1/lib/node_modules/openowl/.owl/owl-darwin-arm64 is not granted macOS Accessibility permission.

Evidence:
  - mcp__owl__screenshot: "Timed out after 5s capturing screenshot. Display may be unresponsive."
  - mcp__owl__get_focused_element: "Focus info unavailable. ApplicationServices not available"
  - mcp__owl__list_windows reported a window titled "Accessibility Access" (system prompt asking to approve Owl 0.1.198 for Accessibility, with [Open System Settings] / [Deny] buttons)

What still worked: WebFetch, PDF generation, mcp__owl__list_windows, mcp__owl__focus_window.

What failed: any Owl action that requires Screen Recording or Accessibility (screenshot, click, type, send_keys, find_element).

Fix (manual, one-time):
  System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility → enable for the Owl binary above. Then also Privacy & Security → Screen Recording → enable for the same binary. After granting, restart Owl or just re-run the daily routine.

